        "subject": "LU-21061 lmv: track MDT pool members on clients",
        "message": "LU-21061 lmv: track MDT pool members on clients\n\nTo place new directories on the MDTs of a pool, a client needs to\nknow which MDTs the pool lists.  The config log only has pool\nrecords for the client LOV, and LMV has no pool operations.\n\nAdd o_pool_new/del/add/rem to LMV, keeping the MDT members of each\npool and ignoring OST members.  When class_process_config() applies\na pool record to a \"-clilov\" device, apply it to the \"-clilmv\"\ndevice of the same mount too, as is done for LCFG_ADD_MDC.  Give\neach pool a reference count, so that a user can keep a pool that\npool_destroy takes off the list.  Nothing uses these pools yet;\ndirectory placement follows.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial mdscount=2 mdtcount=4 testlist=ost-pools\nSigned-off-by: Di Wang <diwa@nvidia.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm\nChange-Id: I512a1642a283bf90152d91f33d4519bf1d965c9d\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
